    {
      "caption": "Factorise by grouping",
      "duration_ms": 9000,
      "id": "s2",
      "narration": "Two x plus six plus x y plus three y has no single common factor \u2014 so group it. Take two out of the first pair, y out of the second pair, and the bracket x plus three appears twice. Pull that whole bracket out: x plus three times two plus y.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "title",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 36,
            "text": "Factorise by grouping",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 100
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "start",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 48,
            "tex": "2x + 6 + xy + 3y",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 200
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 1800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "grp",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 44,
            "tex": "= (2x + 6) + (xy + 3y)",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 300
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "fac",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 44,
            "tex": "= 2(x + 3) + y(x + 3)",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 400
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4400,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "fac"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 5600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "ans",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 48,
            "tex": "= (x + 3)(2 + y)",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 480
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6600,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 1000,
          "target": "ans"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7400,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "Spot the common bracket, then pull it out whole"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "Change the subject to x",
      "duration_ms": 8000,
      "id": "s3",
      "narration": "Make x the subject of y equals three x plus five. Undo the recipe in reverse: the plus five goes first \u2014 subtract five from both sides \u2014 then divide by three. x equals y minus five over three.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "title",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 36,
            "text": "Change the subject to x",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 100
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "l1",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 48,
            "tex": "y = 3x + 5",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 210
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2000,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "l2",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 48,
            "tex": "y - 5 = 3x",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 310
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3600,
          "do": "move",
          "dur_ms": 900,
          "target": "l1",
          "to": {
            "x": 150,
            "y": 150
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4800,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#1f7a3a",
            "id": "l3",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 48,
            "tex": "x = \\frac{y - 5}{3}",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 410
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6000,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 1000,
          "target": "l3"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7000,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "Undo in reverse order: minus five first, then divide by three"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "The (a+b)^2 trap",
      "duration_ms": 8000,
      "id": "s4",
      "narration": "A plus b all squared is not a squared plus b squared. Check with a equals two and b equals three: the left side is twenty-five, the right side is thirteen. The full expansion has three terms \u2014 the secondary A binomial sample shows where the middle term comes from.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at_ms": 0,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "title",
            "kind": "text",
            "size": 36,
            "text": "The (a+b)^2 trap",
            "x": 120,
            "y": 100
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 600,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "color": "#b00020",
            "id": "trap",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 52,
            "tex": "(a + b)^2 \\neq a^2 + b^2",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 210
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 2200,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "ce",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 40,
            "tex": "a = 2,\\; b = 3:\\quad (2 + 3)^2 = 25",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 320
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 3400,
          "do": "show",
          "shape": {
            "id": "ce2",
            "kind": "latex",
            "size": 40,
            "tex": "2^2 + 3^2 = 4 + 9 = 13",
            "x": 150,
            "y": 410
          }
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 4800,
          "do": "emphasize",
          "dur_ms": 1000,
          "target": "trap"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 6000,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "(a+b)^2 expands to a^2 + 2ab + b^2 \u2014 three terms, not two"
        },
        {
          "at_ms": 7000,
          "do": "caption",
          "text": "See the secondary A binomial sample for the full expansion"
        }
      ]
    }
